{=============================================================================
  Two-dimensional steady conduction in a square plate
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0341
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Finite-difference solution of the two-dimensional steady conduction
  equation in a square plate: the temperature of every node of the grid is
  the average of its four neighbours, with two edges at 100 C, one edge at
  0 C and one insulated (no temperature gradient), as in the original.

  Inputs : N (number of nodes in the X and Y directions) [-]
  Outputs: T[i,j] (temperature of the node i,j) [C]
  Units  : SI - temperatures in C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : S. A. Klein (Univ. of Wisconsin-Madison), F-Chart Software EES
           example - see README.md
  Status : blocked by CS-GAP-INDEX-VAR (CoolSolve does not resolve an array
           index that is an expression of a model variable: T[N+1,j] and
           T[i,N+1]); the runnable variant
           conduction_2d_square_plate_coolsolve.eescode changes only those
           indices (see README.md)
=============================================================================}

"!Number of nodes in the X and Y directions"
N=25  "number of nodes in the X and Y directions [-]"

"!Energy balance on interior nodes.  Interior nodes run from 1 to N."
duplicate i=1,N
	duplicate j=1,n
		T[i,j]=(T[i+1,j]+T[i-1,j]+T[i,j+1]+T[i,j-1])/4
	end
end

"!Boundary conditions.  Boundary nodes are 0 and N+1."
duplicate  i=0,N+1
	T[i,0]=100          "left hand side set to 100 [C]"
	T[i,N+1]=T[i,N]    "insulated right hand side - no temperature gradient"
end
duplicate j=1,N
	T[0,j]=100          "bottom surface at 100 [C]"
	T[N+1,j]=0          "top surface at 0 [C]"
end
